course: dictionary
lesson: 338
title: Anniversary: a day that comes back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An anniversary is a day that comes exactly one year, or more, after something important happened. People remember it or celebrate it. The context helps you find this meaning: «Families celebrate wedding anniversaries with cards or a meal» tells you people mark the day on purpose.
explain: Look for clue words. «Wedding» tells you the important event. A number tells you how many years have passed: «the Evanses invite the whole street to their fortieth anniversary» means forty years after the day they married or started something special.
explain: Some anniversaries are sad. «On the anniversary of a loved one's death, families may visit the grave or light a candle.» The clues are visit and candle, which show a day of remembering, not a party. Ask yourself: what are the people doing? That tells you what kind of day it is.
fact: An anniversary is the day exactly one or more years after an important event.
fact: A wedding anniversary is the day each year when a married couple remembers their wedding.
fact: A sad anniversary is the day remembering a death or disaster.
fact: «Grief often returns on birthdays, anniversaries and holidays; this is normal.»
fact: In maths, anniversaries count whole years: the first, second and third anniversary.
exercise: «The Evanses invite the whole street to their fortieth anniversary.» What is an anniversary here? | A type of ice lolly | A street party with no reason at all | A game played at bingo | *The day forty years after an important day they remember
exercise: «On the anniversary of a loved one's death, families may visit the grave or light a candle.» What do families do on this day? | Hold a bingo night in the park | Play in the snow | Go shopping for a new car | *Remember their loved one, for example by lighting a candle
exercise: «The Evanses invite the whole street to their fortieth anniversary.» Find and copy the word that tells you how many years have passed. | whole | invite | street | *fortieth
test: «Grief often returns on birthdays, anniversaries and holidays; this is normal.» What does this tell you about anniversaries? | They are the same thing as holidays | They are always happy days with cake | *They can bring back strong feelings, and that is normal | They only happen once in a life
test: Which is a wedding anniversary? | The day a married couple is born | *The day each year when a married couple remembers their wedding | The day a married couple moves house | A prize won at bingo
exam: Which day is a sad anniversary? | The day you get a new pet | *The day families remember a death or disaster | The day of a school sports race | A day with no reason at all
